{% comment %}
Stage 1 of the decider — per step (a kept step, already built, is not asked) ONE choice (which module does the main work; the options are the
bare module names, their descriptions are in the state once) and a yes/no per common action, with
what yes and no mean (decider.json). Keys and wording are the eval's (tools/decider/harness.py
stage1_questions); a twin test holds the two equal.
Needs: goal, modules (%!app.module.list%), decider (decider.json).
{% endcomment %}
{%- assign names = modules | map: "Name" | sort -%}
{
{%- assign sep = "" -%}
{%- for s in goal.Step -%}
{%- if s.IsKept -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign text = s.Text -%}
{%- capture id %}s{{ s.Index }}_@module{% endcapture -%}
{%- capture ask %}Step {{ s.Index }} of this goal is `{{ text }}`. Which plang module does the main work of step {{ s.Index }}?{% endcapture %}
{{ sep }}
  {{ id | json }}: {
    "type": "choice",
    "criteria": {
{%- assign osep = "" -%}
{%- for m in names -%}
{{ osep }}{{ m | json }}: null
{%- assign osep = ", " -%}
{%- endfor -%}
},
    "instructions": {{ ask | json }}
  }
{%- for c in decider.common -%}
{%- capture id %}s{{ s.Index }}_{{ c[0] }}{% endcapture -%}
{%- capture ask %}Step {{ s.Index }} is `{{ text }}`. Does step {{ s.Index }} use `{{ c[0] }}`?{% endcapture %},
  {{ id | json }}: {
    "type": "noul",
    "instructions": {{ ask | json }},
{%- assign yes = c[1].true | append: "" -%}
{%- assign no = c[1].false | append: "" %}
    "criteria": {"true": {{ yes | json }}, "false": {{ no | json }}}
  }
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign sep = "," -%}
{%- endfor %}
}
